From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Reinstate the NotifyIcon system tray on Gtk4

Gtk4 removed GtkStatusIcon with no replacement, which left NotifyIcon inert:
a permanently-null statusIcon field, a Visible property that only round-tripped
a backing field, and a fabricated 1x1 Gtk.Window standing in for balloon tips.

What GtkStatusIcon actually was, however, is three platform backends behind one
object. This rewires NotifyIcon onto INotifyIconBackend and its three
implementations (Shell_NotifyIcon on Windows, the StatusNotifierItem and
com.canonical.dbusmenu D-Bus protocols on Linux, NSStatusItem on macOS), which
ship as Resources/ overlays copied in by ResourcesCopyService.

Also adds IsSystemTrayAvailable, because a tray is optional on Linux in a way
it never was on Windows - stock GNOME Shell registers no StatusNotifierWatcher -
and silently doing nothing would otherwise be indistinguishable from a bug.

The fake-window balloon is removed: balloon tips are now real desktop
notifications through each platform's notification service.
